---
import EnergyFigure from "./EnergyFigure.astro";
import monthly from "../../../data/interactive/west-energy-bill/monthly-cpi.json";
import { pulseSvg, pulseSeries, rebaseCpi, pulseChange, monthNames } from "../../../lib/interactive/energy/pulse-model";
import "../../../styles/energy-pulse.css";
const rebased = rebaseCpi(monthly.rows);
---

<aside class="energy-pulse" aria-label="Western consumer energy prices" data-energy-pulse>
  <EnergyFigure id="energy-price-pulse">
    <div class="pulse-orientation">
      <p class="energy-kicker">Since the disruption</p>
      <p class="pulse-context">West-region CPI-U · February 2026 = 100</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pulse-visual" data-pulse-visual>
      <Fragment set:html={pulseSvg(monthly.rows, "pulse-wide")} />
      <Fragment set:html={pulseSvg(monthly.rows, "pulse-narrow", true)} />
    </div>
    <div class="pulse-mobile-labels" aria-label="Change from February to August 2026">
      <p>Change since February · August 2026</p>
      {pulseSeries.map(series => <div style={`--series-color:${series.color}`}>
        <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{series.name}</span>
        <strong>{pulseChange(rebased[6][series.key])}</strong>
      </div>)}
    </div>
  </EnergyFigure>
  <details class="energy-data">
    <summary>See monthly data and method</summary>
    <p>Each series divides its monthly BLS index by its February 2026 index and multiplies by 100. Monthly observations cover the whole month, not a specific day. The event marker falls between February and March. The West comprises Alaska, Arizona, California, Colorado, Hawaii, Idaho, Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, Oregon, Utah, Washington, and Wyoming.</p>
    <div class="pulse-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Monthly CPI data; scroll horizontally if needed">
      <table>
        <caption>February 2026 = 100 · raw BLS indexes in parentheses</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">2026</th>{pulseSeries.map(s => <th scope="col">{s.name}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rebased.map((row, i) => <tr><th scope="row">{monthNames[i]}</th>{pulseSeries.map(s => <td>{row[s.key].toFixed(1)} <span>({monthly.rows[i][s.key].toFixed(3)})</span></td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Raw indexes use the BLS 1982–84=100 base. Sources: {monthly.sources.map((source, i) => <><a href={source.url}>BLS {source.id} release</a>{i < monthly.sources.length - 1 ? " · " : ""}</>)}. <a href="/downloads/west-energy-bill/monthly-cpi.csv" download>Download monthly data (CSV)</a>.</p>
  </details>
</aside>
